MAMBA-NIKE NGCC API Implementations
====================================

1. Reference Implementation
---------------------------
Portable C99 implementation used as the canonical KAT source.  Polynomial
multiplication uses coefficient-domain Toom-Cook-4 followed by negacyclic
folding and the q-1 mask.

2. Optimized Implementation
---------------------------
The x86-64 AVX2 build keeps the same protocol and external encoding but uses:

  - AVX2 ChaCha20 assembly for noise-stream generation;
  - poly_mul_small(), a fixed-loop direct negacyclic multiplication backend;
  - four 256-bit accumulators, processing 64 output coefficients per block;
  - 16-bit lane wraparound followed by one q-1 mask.

No secret coefficient is skipped, and the accessed addresses depend only on
the public ring dimension and loop indices.  When AVX2 is disabled, the same
source uses the existing Toom-Cook-4 fallback.

Build Commands
--------------
  # Reference
  cd Reference_Implementation/MAMBA-NIKE-128
  make clean && make
  ./KAT_KEX

  # Optimized AVX2
  cd Optimized_Implementation/MAMBA-NIKE-128
  make clean && make AVX2=1
  ./KAT_KEX

  # Optimized portable fallback
  make clean && make AVX2=0

KAT Rule
--------
Reference is the only canonical KAT generator.  Every Optimized profile must
match the corresponding file under ../../Test_Vectors/ byte for byte.

Frozen Constraints
------------------
The current optimization does not modify parameters.json, profile-specific
params.h files, protocol semantics, or the KAT format.  The submitted package
contains only the Reference and Optimized x86 tracks.  AVX-512, NEON, and
further SHAKE/SIMD work are out of scope.
